{title: 293 - Heavenly Father, Bless Us Now}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #293 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 293}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]Heavenly Father, bless [Gm/Bb]us [Am]now;
[Dm]At the [C]cross [Am]of Christ [E7]we [Am]bow;
[Dm]Take our [Gm]guilt and [C]grief away;
[F]Hear and [C]heal [Dm]us [Am]now, we [Dm]pray.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm]Now, O Lord, [A/Db]this [Dm]very [Am]hour,
[Dm]Send Thy grace [C]and [Am]show Thy [E7]power;
[Dm]While we [Gm]rest upon [C]Thy [F]word,
[F]Come, and [C]bless [Dm]us [Am]now, O [Dm]Lord!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm]Mercy now, [A/Db]O [Dm]Lord, [Gm/Bb]we [Am]plead
[Dm]In this [C]hour [Am]of utter need;
[Dm]Turn us [Gm]not away [C]unblest;
[F]Calm our [C]anguish [Am]into [Dm]rest.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Dm]O Thou loving, blessed [Gm/Bb]One,
[Dm]Rising [C]o'er [Am]us like [E7]the [Am]sun,
[Dm]Light and [Gm]life art [C]Thou within:
[F]Savior, Thou, [C]from [Dm]every sin!
{end_of_verse}
